course: dictionary
lesson: 358
title: Antelope: a wild animal with horns
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antelope is a fast, graceful wild animal, a bit like a deer, with horns. Most antelopes live in Africa and Asia. It is a noun, and you can say one antelope or many antelopes.
explain: The sentences give you clues. «Lions and cheetahs hunt antelopes» tells you antelopes are animals that other animals eat. «A herd of antelope» tells you they often live in groups. Check your meaning by swapping in "animal": «Lions and cheetahs hunt animals» still makes sense, so you are on track.
explain: Some sentences in this lesson are jokes. «An antelope with a little trunk» comes from a drawing made for a laugh. The dictionary tells you what real antelopes are like: wild animals with horns, not trunks. Gazelle, impala and gnu are all real kinds of antelope.
fact: An antelope is a fast, graceful wild animal, like a deer, with horns.
fact: Most antelopes live in Africa and Asia.
fact: Gazelle, impala and gnu are all kinds of antelope.
fact: «Energy passes from grass to antelopes to lions» shows that antelopes are food for lions in a food chain.
fact: Gazelles sometimes bounce on stiff legs, called pronking or stotting, which may tell a hunter «I am fit, don't chase me».
exercise: «Energy passes from grass to antelopes to lions.» In this food chain, what is an antelope? | A decomposer | A plant | A kind of soil | *An animal that lions eat
exercise: Which of these is a kind of antelope? | Giraffe | Cheetah | *Gazelle | Lion
exercise: «A herd of antelope» suggests that antelopes often live | Alone, far from others | *In groups | Up in trees | Under the sea
test: Which continents are most antelopes found in? | Europe and Australia | Antarctica | South America | *Africa and Asia
test: Gnu, impala and gazelle are all what? | Lions | Pine cones | Decomposers | *Antelopes
exam: Which statement is a real fact about antelopes, not a joke? | A bird has a shoe for a beak | An antelope has a little trunk like an elephant | *An antelope is a wild animal with horns that lives mainly in Africa and Asia | An antelope is a walking pine cone
